WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.535
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with John Oliver.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
John, I've always
appreciated over the years

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
that if you text me
about something we've done

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.673 line:92%
on the show, it is something

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:09.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
that no one else has liked
or commented on.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:14.147
I felt that way about your
long-running Adam Driver bit

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:17.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
that came to a wonderful
conclusion with Adam Driver.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yes.
-Can you just talk us

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the beginning of it,
the seeds of where it started,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the conclusion of getting
the real Adam Driver?

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, the seed --
the initial seed was,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, one of our writers
writing a very weird joke

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:33.099 line:92%
out of absolutely nowhere.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:35.368 line:92%
And then the water on that see

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:39.272 size:78% position:39%
was, back when we had
an audience in March,

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
feeling real resistance
from the audience at the joke.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
It felt like they
about 40% enjoyed it.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.148 line:92%
And it logged in my head -

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, let's try
and do this again."

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we did it as a callback
a few weeks later,

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they weren't really happ
to have it back.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:57.991 line:92%
And so at that point, it becam

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
something of an obsession
in our staff.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:07.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a few months into the bit,
we kind of -- we broke it.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the writers had written
something kind of saying,

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:10.970 line:92%
"I don't know if he even -

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't seem like
he would enjoy this one.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It could be over."

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:17.243
That was as much of a ribbon
as it felt we could put on it.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
So at that point,
we reached out to him and said

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.915
"I don't know if you know
what we've been doing.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no easy way
into this conversation.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've been making some comment
about you,

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
and would you hypothetically
be interested

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:35.328 size:78% position:39%
in responding towards
the end of the year?"

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the message came back
from him saying

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:43.803
he has heard about it, he thinks
it's very strange, and he's in

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.004 line:92%
So I thought, "Oh, great."

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:47.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we didn't know what we were
going to do, but at least

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
we knew at that point
that we had an end in sight.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, as it turned out,
what the end in sight was

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.915 line:92%
was him calling into the sho

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.686
and explaining the ways in which
he was going to demolish me.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.321 line:92%
-It was also -- Watching i

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:05.425
is a real reminder that
Adam Driver is a terrific actor.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Unbelievably good.
I couldn't see him.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was doing it --
I could only hear him,

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it wasn't until
I watched it back, you think

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.167 line:92%
"Oh, [bleep]. Look at him!

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.736
Look at him doing acting,
as I'm giving him nothing back."

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, he's literally performin
in front of a tennis ball.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:22.809
That's the equivalent of wha
he's getting back from me.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.546
And he's doing such good acting.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:30.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At a point where
it really was not required

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he was really
flexing muscles.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:37.090
-Yeah. It was a case -- An
I say this as a fan of yours

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you guys
were on the split screen,

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:42.061
it was very hard to imagin
anyone was watching you.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:46.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't be 100% confident
it was there.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.836 size:78% position:39%
It was -- Every part
of that juxtaposition

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:52.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
is [bleep] brutal.
-Yeah.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Acting ability, physically.
Let's not lie.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.509 line:92%
Put those two things together,

00:02:56.509 --> 00:03:00.513
and it barely seems like
the same species -- barely

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.415 line:92%
